From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:36:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Run timers on a world's tick thread, and record calls from
 the wrong thread

Athena.runOnWorldTimer's tasks are kept by the world and run at the start of its
tick (MinecraftServer.athenaTickWorld), on its own thread or on the server
thread, counting the world's own ticks; others hand new ones over through a
queue, and unloading the world cancels them.

A test aid for the long runs: with -Dathena.threadCheck=true, block changes,
entity adds, removes, kills and moves, chunk loads and lookups, the entity
tracker and the player chunk map record each call from a thread that does not
tick their world, and calls AsyncCatcher refuses. Each place is logged once with
its stack and counted; the server logs the summary when it stops. Off, the
checks are a constant false and compile away.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

